-- title:
--   Intrinsic kernel characterization on any finite ambient coordinate type
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Foundations.Introspection.AuxiliaryDualKernel` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). Coordinate-independent kernel tests for auxiliary dual answers. The semantic dual uses a chosen local enumeration, but equality of its outputs is characterized intrinsically by the ambient dot product. The general finite index API permits coordinate transport without transporting chosen complements.
--
--   Intrinsic kernel characterization on any finite ambient coordinate type.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.Introspection
--   open MIPRE.Introspection.AuxiliaryDual
--   open Finset
--   variable {F ι : Type*} [Field F] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {S : Finset ι}
--
--   theorem MIPRE.Introspection.AuxiliaryDual.registerDual_zero_iff_dot (L : CL.RegLinear F S) (x : ι → F) :
--       registerDual L x = 0 ↔ ∀ y : ι → F, L y = 0 → ∑ i, y i * CL.proj S x i = 0
